Source: hermes-net
Section: network
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Rafael Diniz <rafael@rhizomatica.org>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 12),
               libb64-dev, liblzma-dev, zlib1g-dev,
               libiniparser-dev, libi2c-dev, libssl-dev, libasound2-dev,
               libfftw3-dev, csdr
Standards-Version: 4.5.0
Homepage: www.rhizomatica.org/hermes

Package: uucpd
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: uucp (>= 1.07-37)
Description: HERMES network subsystem: UUCP over the HF modem
 uucpd and uuport, which carry UUCP over an HF modem's TNC (Mercury or
 VARA); uuxcomp and the HERMES e-mail, image and audio compression helpers;
 the uucpd service, with its options in /etc/default/uucpd; the ALSA
 loopback routing the modem uses; and the sBitx i2c device name.
 .
 It works with either radio controller, sbitx-controller or
 hermes-radio-daemon, and installs neither.  uucp 1.07-37 or later adds the
 pre-agreed startup (uucpd -F).

Package: sbitx-controller
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: HERMES sBitx radio controller (sbitx_controller)
 The original HERMES controller for the sBitx: sbitx_controller,
 sbitx_client, sbitx.service and its configuration in /etc/sbitx.
 .
 hermes-radio-daemon supersedes it.  The two drive the same radio and
 cannot run at once, so sbitx.service conflicts with radiod.service.
